{
  // Type-checks every test file in the workspace. Nothing else does.
  //
  // Each `packages/*/tsconfig.json` and `games/*/tsconfig.json` excludes `*.test.ts` (correctly —
  // tests must not be emitted into `dist`), vitest transpiles without type-checking, and eslint is
  // not type-aware. The net effect was that `npm run verify` never type-checked a single test file,
  // so a fixture could silently drift out of contract with the type it claims to exercise. That is
  // exactly what had happened: `packages/mode-fps/src/systems.test.ts` had been building malformed
  // `InputFrame`s since the file was written, and only passed because no system read the missing
  // fields. See docs/working-agreement.md §3.
  //
  // This is a check-only program: `noEmit`, no `composite`, no declarations. It never contributes
  // to `tsc -b` output and cannot pollute `dist`.
  //
  // The root `test/` entry covers repository-level checks that belong to no single package —
  // today, the guard that every code template in `AGENTS.md` is still a verbatim quote of a file
  // the gate runs. It is listed here for the same reason as everything else: a test directory
  // that nothing type-checks is a test directory that can drift.
  //
  // Deliberate trade-off: this is ONE program covering every project, so `lib` and `types` are the
  // union of what the individual projects need (DOM for render-three/cli, node for anything
  // touching `node:*`). A `packages/core` test could therefore reference `document` without a type
  // error. That is a far smaller hole than not type-checking tests at all, and it is not silent —
  // such a test fails immediately at runtime under vitest's node environment.
  //
  // `@aegis/*` specifiers resolve through the workspace symlinks to each package's built
  // `dist/*.d.ts`, i.e. against the real published contract. That needs a build first, which is why
  // `verify` runs `build` before `typecheck:tests` and why this config has a `pretypecheck:tests`
  // hook in the root package.json for standalone runs.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "composite": false,
    "declaration": false,
    "declarationMap": false,
    "sourceMap": false,
    "types": ["node"],
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"]
  },
  "include": [
    "packages/*/src/**/*.test.ts",
    "packages/*/src/**/*.spec.ts",
    "packages/*/test/**/*.ts",
    "games/*/src/**/*.test.ts",
    "games/*/src/**/*.spec.ts",
    "games/*/test/**/*.ts",
    "test/**/*.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": ["**/dist/**", "**/node_modules/**"]
}
